GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=placeholder
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=placeholder
```

## 9. Dashboard page (protected route)

`src/app/dashboard/page.tsx`:
```tsx
import { getCurrentUser, listUsers } from "@/lib/users";

export default async function DashboardPage() {
  const me = await getCurrentUser();
  const all = await listUsers();

  return (
    <main className="mx-auto max-w-2xl p-8">
      <h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Dashboard</h1>
      <p className="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">
        Signed in as {me?.name ?? "nobody"} ({me?.email ?? "—"})
      </p>

      <h2 className="mt-8 text-lg font-medium">Team</h2>
      <ul className="mt-2 space-y-1">
        {all.map((u) => (
          <li key={u.id} className="text-sm">
            {u.name} — {u.email} — joined {u.createdAt}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </main>
  );
}
```
It's protected purely by `src/proxy.ts`'s matcher (`/dashboard/:path*`), which redirects unauthenticated requests to `/signin?callbackUrl=/dashboard`.

## 10. Project structure

```
app/                                  (repo root, Next.js App Router project named "scaffold" / app title "Notely")
├── .env.example
├── docs/
│   └── clerk.md                      (untracked — Clerk migration doc, not part of git history)
├── llms.txt                          (untracked — Clerk marketing/llms index)
├── next.config.ts                    (default, no custom config)
├── package.json
├── README.md
├── src/
│   ├── auth.ts                       (NextAuth v5 config: providers, callbacks, session)
│   ├── proxy.ts                      (Next 16's middleware convention; protects /dashboard)
│   ├── lib/
│   │   └── users.ts                  (in-memory user store + auth helper functions)
│   └── app/
│       ├── layout.tsx                (root layout; renders session-aware nav/header)
│       ├── page.tsx                  (default Next.js starter home page, unmodified content)
│       ├── globals.css
│       ├── sign-out-button.tsx       (client component calling next-auth/react signOut)
│       ├── signin/page.tsx
│       ├── signup/page.tsx
│       ├── dashboard/page.tsx        (protected page)
│       └── api/
│           ├── auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts   (NextAuth handlers: GET/POST)
│           └── signup/route.ts               (custom credentials sign-up endpoint)
```

Key architecture notes:
- App Router (`src/app`), TypeScript, Tailwind v4.
- Auth is NextAuth v5 (beta) with two providers: Credentials (bcrypt) and Google OAuth.
- User "database" is a non-persistent in-memory array (`src/lib/users.ts`), globalThis-pinned to survive Turbopack module duplication — explicitly documented in the file's own comments as a workaround, and in README.md ("Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list... There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet" — this README line is stale/out of date relative to the actual code, which does have sign-in).
- Route protection is centralized in `src/proxy.ts` (Next 16's renamed middleware file) and only covers `/dashboard/:path*`.
- No real database, ORM, or schema migrations exist anywhere in the repo.

